          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उत्तीर्ण होणे — uttīrṇa hoṇe — \"to pass (an exam)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अरुण पहिल्या प्रयत्नात परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण झाला. aruṇ pahilyā prayatnāt parīkṣā uttīrṇa jhālā. Arun passed the exam at the first attempt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): तो उत्तीर्ण झाला, to uttīrṇa jhālā."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal; what is passed is the object, with no ending: परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण होणे (uttīrṇa hoṇe)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उत्तीर्ण होणे (uttīrṇa hoṇe) joins the tatsama उत्तीर्ण, Sanskrit uttīrṇa, \"crossed over, landed\" (Monier-Williams), to होणे, \"to become\": to get across."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
